  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the tower-stacking game in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks with the typecheck tool, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so none of the gameplay has been tested.\n\n- **Scene:** `createAuraApp(\"#app\")` with the `product-studio` look. There are 26 pre-built slab boxes and 26 matching \"debris\" boxes, one pair per level. They are moved and resized at runtime with `setPosition`/`setScale`/`setVisible`. Each level has a fixed color whose hue shifts a little per level.\n- **Slab motion:** The current slab slides along x. Its speed starts at 1.5 and rises 0.12 every 3 levels, capped at 3.2.\n- **Drops:** Space or a click drops the slab.\n  - A miss sets `lost`.\n  - Otherwise the overhang is cut off and falls away, and the next slab takes the remaining width.\n  - A drop within 0.08 of the slab below keeps the full width and adds +1 to the score.\n  - The 25th stacked slab sets `won`.\n- **Scoring:** The base slab is not counted. `height` is the number of slabs stacked on top of it, and `score` is `height` plus the bonuses.\n- **Camera:** It rises smoothly with the tower through `app.camera?.setPose`. That call is optional in the types, so if the camera controller isn't available the camera will stay fixed.\n- **Restart:** R restarts at any time, and a click after the game ends also restarts.\n- **HUD and state:** A DOM bar under the canvas shows score, best for the session and status. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated on every change. `window.__TASK_READY__` is set after the first few rendered frames once `app.ready()` has resolved. If `app.ready()` never resolves in headless Chromium, the game won't start and the ready flag stays false.\n\n",
